Independently verify whether each rendered wiki fact is a useful, self-contained representation of its fixed
canonical claim group.

A supported fact must be understandable when read alone under the supplied owner and section, identify the subject
and relevant object or activity, preserve negation, uncertainty, time, quantities, and constraints, and be directly
entailed by every member claim. Mark unsupported when wording depends on unresolved conversational references, omits
the fact's distinguishing subject or object, becomes misleading outside the source turn, or adds unsupported meaning.
Evaluate only the rendered text against the quoted member claims. Do not rewrite facts or regroup claims. Return JSON
matching the schema.
